  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In trivalent state most of the 13th group compounds being covalent are hydrolysed in water. Trichlorides of group 13 on hydrolysis in water form tetrahedral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>−</mo></msup></math> species, the hybridisation state of element <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>In case of aluminium, acidified aqueous solution forms octahedral <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Al</mi><msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ion, which has an aluminium as a central metal atom and water molecules as ligands. The aluminium is in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>  oxidation state and forms<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo> </mo><mn>6</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybrid orbitals. </p><p>Hence option D is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
